SEAM-EXTRACTION: pull the "does this event advance this quest?" decision out of the inline if-ladder and into ONE canonical pure predicate that the reducer calls. Both B6b and B6a are the same seam, so this single module fixes both in one change.

FILE 1 (NEW) — frontend/src/game/questMatch.js (pure, no React/store/side-effects):

  // questMatch.js — the PURE quest-event matcher. One canonical place that decides whether a
  // progress event advances a quest, with correct kill/kill_type semantics.
  //
  // WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS (the bugs it kills):
  //   B6b — the old inline ladder matched a kill_type quest on ANY 'kill_type' event, never checking
  //         quest.mobType === extra.mobType, so one spider kill advanced every targeted hunt.
  //   B6a — the kill path emits BOTH 'kill' and 'kill_type' for one death; the old 'kill' arm matched
  //         both, so every "Defeat N mobs" quest counted each kill twice.
  export function matchesQuestEvent(quest, type, extra = {}) {
    // Any-mob kill quest: advanced by the canonical 'kill' event ONLY. It must NOT also match the
    // per-mob 'kill_type' event, or the double-dispatch below would count one kill twice (B6a).
    if (quest.type === 'kill') return type === 'kill';
    // Targeted hunt: advanced ONLY by a 'kill_type' event whose mob matches — the mob filter is the
    // whole point of the quest (B6b).
    if (quest.type === 'kill_type') return type === 'kill_type' && quest.mobType === extra.mobType;
    // Every other kind: block_place/break, spell_cast, chest_open, reach_shrine, survive_nights.
    return quest.type === type;
  }

