B2h-boss-killblock.fix_plan:
SEAM-EXTRACTION — pull the kill out of the impure updater into (1) a pure health fn + (2) an injectable, throw-isolated effects runner, driven from a post-commit effect.

FILE 1 (NEW) — src/game/bossKill.js:
  export const applyBossDamage = (prev, amount) => Math.max(0, prev - amount);   // pure, no side effects
  export function runBossKillEffects(fx) {
    const failed = [];
    const isolate = (name, fn) => { try { fn?.(); } catch (error) { failed.push({ name, error }); } };
    isolate('defeatUi', fx.defeatUi);   // setBossActive(false)/setBossDefeated(true)/notification
    isolate('grantXp', fx.grantXp);
    isolate('drops', fx.drops);
    isolate('juice', fx.juice);         // hitstop + bloom spike
    fx.markGameWon?.();                  // WIN LATCH LAST + idempotent: no reward failure can void it
    return failed;
  }

FILE 2 — src/world/bossSystem.js:
  a) import { applyBossDamage, runBossKillEffects } from '../game/bossKill.js';
  b) Replace the damageBoss updater body with a PURE one:
        const damageBoss = useCallback((amount) => {
          if (!bossActive || bossHealth <= 0) return;
          setBossHealth(prev => applyBossDamage(prev, amount));   // pure — health only
        }, [bossActive, bossHealth]);
     (Keeping the functional updater preserves same-frame double-hit accuracy, e.g. melee+spell in one frame.)
  c) Add a POST-COMMIT effect keyed on [bossHealth] that fires the kill EXACTLY ONCE and commits the guard LAST:
        useEffect(() => {
          if (bossHealth > 0 || bossKilledRef.current) return;
          const store = useGameStore.getState();
          runBossKillEffects({
            defeatUi: () => { setBossActive(false); setBossDefeated(true); setBossNotification('BOSS DEFEATED! ...'); scheduleNotifClear(6000); },
            grantXp:  () => { if (GameMethods.grantXP) GameMethods.grantXP(BOSS_CONFIG.xpReward, 'Shadow Dragon Defeated!'); },
            drops:    () => { if (store.addToInventory) { store.addToInventory('Crown of the Dragon King', 1); store.addToInventory('Dragon Scale', 3); } },
            juice:    () => { useGameStore.setState({ hitstopUntil: performance.now() + HITSTOP.boss }); if (store.triggerBloomSpike) store.triggerBloomSpike(450); },
            markGameWon: () => { if (store.markGameWon) store.markGameWon(); },
          });
          bossKilledRef.current = true;   // once-guard COMMITTED last — only after the win is latched
        }, [bossHealth]);

Why this is the right seam (not a call-site patch): the updater becomes trivially pure; the store remains the sole owner of the persisted win (markGameWon, no mirror); the throw-isolation + win-last invariant lives in ONE reusable module (bossKill.js) that a unit test can drive directly. Idempotency is preserved by the bossKilledRef guard inside the post-commit effect; the DEV forceBossSpawn already resets bossKilledRef=false, so a re-killed dev boss still works.

