B3b-crystal-blackhole.red_test_content:
// @vitest-environment jsdom
import { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, afterEach } from 'vitest';
import { render, screen, fireEvent, cleanup, within } from '@testing-library/react';
import '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest';
import { TradingInterface } from '../../src/ui/TradingInterface.jsx';
import { SoundProvider } from '../../src/SoundManager.jsx';
import { useGameStore } from '../../src/store/useGameStore.jsx';

// B3b — THE CRYSTAL/WAND BLACK HOLE. Crystals + wands live in TWO buckets: trades and crafting WRITE
// inventory.blocks, but the wand trade, the merchant readout and the cast-time mana discount READ
// inventory.magic. So the loop ore -> crystals -> wand -> cheaper spells never closes:
//   - crystals earned by trading ore are unspendable (the wand trade can't see them),
//   - the "Crystals to Wand" trade is permanently unreachable,
//   - a bought wand gives 0% discount (it lands in blocks.wand; the caster reads magic.wand).
//
// This drives the REAL TradingInterface against the REAL store (no mocks of the trade logic) and asserts
// the loop CLOSES — it is bucket-agnostic (it observes rendered UI + the shared accessor), so it holds
// whichever bucket the fix canonicalizes on, as long as every reader/writer shares ONE accessor.
//
// MUTATION-PROOF: in src/game/crystalWallet.js make getCrystals read a DIFFERENT section than
// earnCrystals writes (re-split the bucket) and the first test goes RED.

const ORIGINAL_INV = useGameStore.getState().inventory;
const ORIGINAL_COINS = useGameStore.getState().coins;

beforeEach(() => {
  // Both crystal buckets and both wand buckets start empty; plenty of gold to earn crystals from ore
  // (Gold -> Crystal costs 2 gold, grants 1 crystal). The test controls the inventory precisely, so it
  // is independent of where the starting loadout seeds crystals/wands.
  useGameStore.setState({ coins: 0, inventory: { blocks: { gold: 100 }, tools: {}, magic: {} } });
});
afterEach(() => {
  cleanup();
  useGameStore.setState({ inventory: ORIGINAL_INV, coins: ORIGINAL_COINS });
});

// TradingInterface calls useGameSounds() -> needs SoundProvider context (jsdom has no AudioContext, so
// the sound calls are guarded no-ops). Same wiring the existing integration test uses.
const renderTrade = () => render(
  <TradingInterface villager={{ npcName: 'Bram the Trader' }} onClose={() => {}} />,
  { wrapper: SoundProvider }
);

// The "Trade" button belonging to the row whose label is `name` — robust to trade reordering / Panel nesting.
function tradeRowFor(name) {
  let row = screen.getByText(name).parentElement;
  while (row && !within(row).queryByRole('button', { name: /^trade$/i })) row = row.parentElement;
  if (!row) throw new Error(`No Trade button row found for "${name}"`);
  return row;
}
const tradeButtonFor = (name) => within(tradeRowFor(name)).getByRole('button', { name: /^trade$/i });
const clickTradeFor = (name) => fireEvent.click(tradeButtonFor(name));

describe('B3b crystal/wand black hole — the ore -> crystals -> wand -> mana loop must close', () => {
  it('crystals earned by trading ore are spendable on the wand trade (ONE bucket, not two)', () => {
    renderTrade();

    // Control: broke, so the wand trade is unaffordable and disabled.
    expect(tradeButtonFor('Crystals to Wand')).toBeDisabled();

    // Earn 15 crystals by trading ore (Crystals -> Wand costs 15).
    for (let i = 0; i < 15; i++) clickTradeFor('Gold to Crystal');

    // The crystals just earned MUST make the wand trade affordable.
    // RED today: ore trades bank blocks.crystals, but the wand trade reads magic.crystals (still 0).
    expect(tradeButtonFor('Crystals to Wand')).toBeEnabled();
  });

  it('a merchant-bought wand powers the SAME mana discount the caster reads (end-to-end)', () => {
    renderTrade();

    expect(screen.getByText('-0% spell mana')).toBeInTheDocument(); // no wand focus yet

    for (let i = 0; i < 15; i++) clickTradeFor('Gold to Crystal'); // earn the 15 crystals...
    clickTradeFor('Crystals to Wand');                              // ...and buy the wand

    // One owned wand = a 6% mana discount (WAND_MANA_PER=0.06). The merchant preview reads the same
    // wand field the caster (EnhancedMagicSystem) charges from.
    // RED today: the wand landed in blocks.wand; the preview + the caster both read magic.wand -> still -0%.
    expect(screen.getByText('-6% spell mana')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('the bought wand + leftover crystals live in the ONE bucket the discount reader consumes', async () => {
    // The seam module the fix introduces — the single accessor every reader/writer shares. Importing it
    // here pins that a wand bought at the merchant is visible to exactly the value the caster discounts on.
    const { getWands, getCrystals } = await import('../../src/game/crystalWallet.js');
    const { applyWandFocus } = await import('../../src/game/wandFocus.js');

    renderTrade();
    for (let i = 0; i < 15; i++) clickTradeFor('Gold to Crystal');
    clickTradeFor('Crystals to Wand');

    const inv = useGameStore.getState().inventory;
    expect(getCrystals(inv)).toBe(0); // 15 earned − 15 spent on the wand
    expect(getWands(inv)).toBe(1);    // the bought wand is exactly where the caster looks
    expect(applyWandFocus(20, getWands(inv))).toBeLessThan(20); // ...and it actually discounts mana
  });
});

B3b-crystal-blackhole.fix_plan:
SEAM EXTRACTION: introduce ONE canonical crystal/wand accessor and make trade-in, trade-out, craft and the mana-discount consumer all go through it. Canonical bucket = inventory.blocks — it is the flat bucket the Inventory panel already renders (magic is rendered NOWHERE, per startingLoadout.test.js:8 and inventory-flat-bucket-gates:11), and addToInventory + all crafting already write blocks. So the WRITES are already correct; the drift is entirely on the READ/SPEND/SEED side pointing at magic.

1) NEW FILE src/game/crystalWallet.js — pure, node-testable, no store/React import:
   export const CRYSTAL_KEY = 'crystals';
   export const WAND_KEY = 'wand';
   export const getCrystals = (inv) => inv?.blocks?.[CRYSTAL_KEY] || 0;
   export const getWands    = (inv) => inv?.blocks?.[WAND_KEY]    || 0;
   const bump = (inv, key, d) => ({ ...inv, blocks: { ...inv?.blocks, [key]: Math.max(0, (inv?.blocks?.[key] || 0) + d) } });
   export const earnCrystals  = (inv, n = 1) => bump(inv, CRYSTAL_KEY,  n);
   export const spendCrystals = (inv, n = 1) => bump(inv, CRYSTAL_KEY, -n);
   export const earnWands     = (inv, n = 1) => bump(inv, WAND_KEY,     n);

2) src/store/useGameStore.jsx:587-596 — move the seed OUT of the vestigial magic bucket into the canonical one: add `crystals: 8, wand: 1` to the `blocks: {…}` object and set `magic: {}`. Store still owns the persisted state (no mirror). (This also finally makes the starting crystals/wand visible in the Inventory panel.)

3) src/EnhancedMagicSystem.jsx:175 — the CONSUMER: `import { getWands } from './game/wandFocus'`… no — `import { getWands } from './game/crystalWallet';` and change to
   `const manaCost = applyWandFocus(baseManaCost, getWands(useGameStore.getState().inventory));`
   This is the load-bearing read: it must consume the SAME accessor the trade writes.

4) src/ui/TradingInterface.jsx — replace every magic-bucket read with the accessor; route the wand SPEND through spendCrystals. Keep the wand GRANT (line 66 `[magicItem]: (prev.blocks[magicItem]||0)+resultCount`) — it is already blocks.wand:
   - import `{ getCrystals, getWands, spendCrystals } from '../game/crystalWallet'` (keep wandManaMultiplier).
   - :48 eligibility -> `const currentCrystals = getCrystals(gameState.inventory);`
   - :58-68 executeCrystalTrade -> spend canonical crystals, grant wand into blocks:
       gameState.setInventory(prev => ({ ...spendCrystals(prev, requiredCrystals),
         blocks: { ...spendCrystals(prev, requiredCrystals).blocks, [magicItem]: (prev.blocks[magicItem]||0)+resultCount } }));
     (or simpler: compute `const next = spendCrystals(prev, requiredCrystals); return { ...next, blocks: { ...next.blocks, [magicItem]: (next.blocks[magicItem]||0)+resultCount } };`)
   - :144 display -> `{getCrystals(gameState.inventory)}` ; :148 -> `{getWands(gameState.inventory)}` ; :151 -> `wandManaMultiplier(getWands(gameState.inventory))`.
   - :180-182 currentStock for crystal rows -> `getCrystals(gameState.inventory)` (drop the `magic` local at :21).
   - executeBlockTrade (:24-45) already banks blocks.crystals (canonical) — leave, or route the crystal grant through earnCrystals for symmetry.

5) src/ui/panels/CraftingTable.jsx / src/data/recipes.js — no change: the "Magic Crystal" recipe already flows crystals into blocks via addToInventory (now the canonical bucket end-to-end).

Net: getCrystals/getWands become the single choke every reader shares; a bucket rename or drift is now a one-line change in crystalWallet.js that the gate catches.
